{"t": 1794116708.2809937, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": "reports-api 502s \u2014 root cause found and fixed in reports/export.py.\n\nCause: upstream ledger 2026.11 added a `currency` field to every row. The CSV exporter declared only `id,amount`, so csv.DictWriter raised ValueError: \"dict contains fields not in fieldnames: 'currency'\" on every export request (visible in CloudWatch /ecs/reports-api).\n\nFix: added `currency` to the export fieldnames (id, amount, currency). Verified locally with new rows (id/amount/currency), legacy rows without currency, and empty input \u2014 no exception.\n\nStatus: code change ready in reports/export.py; needs the normal reports-api deploy/restart to take effect. No data loss \u2014 existing id/amount values are unchanged."}, "ok": true}
